                <pb facs="0751" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg631"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root advises Mr. Morgan that the representation of the United States in
                    diplomatic matters affecting American treaty rights, persons, or property in
                    Korea is transferred to the American legation at Tokyo, where such questions
                    will be negotiated through the Japanese foreign office. Instructs him to
                    transfer the legation property and archives to the custody of the
                    consul-general; to withdraw from Korea and to return to the United States.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
